PathwayData.put("data/grammar_vocabulary/units/L04U1.json",{"strand":"grammar_vocabulary","level":4,"cefr":"A2b","unit":1,"theme":"Record Breakers","essential_question":"What makes something the biggest, the fastest or the best?","lessons":[{"id":"GV-L04-U1-LS1","title":"The Tallest Building in the World: Superlative Adjectives","objectives":["Students will be able to form superlatives with -est and the most.","Students will be able to use superlatives to describe records with in the world / in the class.","I can say \"the tallest building in the world\".","I can say \"the most interesting fact\" and \"the best day\"."],"objectives_ar":["سيتمكن الطلاب من تكوين صيغة التفضيل بـ est وthe most.","سيتمكن الطلاب من استخدام صيغ التفضيل لوصف الأرقام القياسية مع in the world / in the class.","أستطيع أن أقول the tallest building in the world.","أستطيع أن أقول the most interesting fact وthe best day."],"vocabulary":[{"word":"record","pos":"noun","ipa":"/rəˈkɔrd/","definition":"the best result that anyone has ever had","arabic":"رقم قياسي","example":"She broke the school record for running.","image_id":"GV-L04-U1-LS1-W01","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L04-U1-LS1-W01"},{"word":"champion","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈtʃæmpiən/","definition":"a person or team that wins a competition","arabic":"بطل","example":"The champion lifted the gold cup.","image_id":"GV-L04-U1-LS1-W02","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L04-U1-LS1-W02"},{"word":"height","pos":"noun","ipa":"/haɪt/","definition":"how tall or high something is","arabic":"ارتفاع / طول","example":"The height of the tower is 828 meters.","image_id":"GV-L04-U1-LS1-W03","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L04-U1-LS1-W03"},{"word":"length","pos":"noun","ipa":"/lɛŋkθ/","definition":"how long something is","arabic":"طول","example":"The length of the river is 6,650 kilometers.","image_id":"GV-L04-U1-LS1-W04","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L04-U1-LS1-W04"}],"explanation":{"text":"We use superlatives to compare one thing with all the others in a group (three or more): The cheetah is the fastest animal on land.\nShort adjectives: the + adjective + -est: tall → the tallest. Long adjectives: the most + adjective: interesting → the most interesting.\nAlways use the before a superlative. After it we often say in + place/group (in the world, in my class) or of + a number/time (of the three, of the year).\nshort: the + adj + -est: high → the highest\nlong: the most + adj: famous → the most famous\nirregular: good → the best • bad → the worst • far → the farthest\nin the world / in my family • of all / of the year","examples":["Mount Everest is the highest mountain in the world.","My grandfather is the oldest person in our family.","Riyadh is the largest city in Saudi Arabia.","This is the most delicious cake I have ever eaten.","Saturday was the best day of the trip.","That was the worst storm of the year.","The giraffe is the tallest animal on Earth.","Which is the most expensive car in the shop?"],"common_errors":["✗ Burj Khalifa is tallest building. → ✓ The Burj Khalifa is the tallest building. (Use the before a superlative.)","✗ He is the most tall boy in the class. → ✓ He is the tallest boy in the class. (Short adjective → -est.)","✗ She is the goodest student. → ✓ She is the best student. (good → the best.)","✗ It's the biggest city of Saudi Arabia. → ✓ It's the biggest city in Saudi Arabia. (Use in with places.)"],"arabic":"نستخدم صيغة التفضيل لمقارنة شيء واحد بكل الأشياء الأخرى في مجموعة: the fastest (الأسرع).\nالصفة القصيرة: the + الصفة + est، والطويلة: the most + الصفة.\nلا بد من the قبل صيغة التفضيل، ونستخدم in مع الأماكن: in the world.\nصيغ شاذة: the best (الأفضل) وthe worst (الأسوأ)."},"video":{"script":[{"time":"00:00–00:20","narration":"Hi, I’m Zaki! Today’s lesson is “The Tallest Building in the World: Superlative Adjectives”. Let’s learn superlative adjectives (the -est / the most …; the best, the worst) together.","on_screen":"GV-L04-U1-LS1 | The Tallest Building in the World: Superlative Adjectives","visual":"Zaki the Falcon flies in over the Leaf Green title card and lands next to the lesson title; soft chime."},{"time":"00:20–00:45","narration":"Listen to the start of “Amazing Record Facts”: Omar loves amazing facts, so he made a poster for his class. The tallest building in the world is the Burj Khalifa in Dubai. It is 828 meters high! The highest fountain in the world is King Fahd's Fountain in Jeddah. Look at the green words.","on_screen":"Omar loves amazing facts, so he made a poster for his class. The tallest building in the world is the Burj Khalifa in Dubai. It is 828 meters high! The highest fountain in the world is King Fahd's Fountain in Jeddah.","visual":"Image GV-L04-U1-LS1-IMG01 animates gently; target words glow Leaf Green as they are spoken."},{"time":"00:45–01:30","narration":"We use superlatives to compare one thing with all the others in a group (three or more): The cheetah is the fastest animal on land. Short adjectives: the + adjective + -est: tall → the tallest. Long adjectives: the most + adjective: interesting → the most interesting.","on_screen":"short: the + adj + -est: high → the highest • long: the most + adj: famous → the most famous • irregular: good → the best • bad → the worst • far → the farthest","visual":"Grammar box builds line by line (form → meaning → use); Zaki points to each line."},{"time":"01:30–02:15","narration":"Here are some examples. Mount Everest is the highest mountain in the world. My grandfather is the oldest person in our family. Riyadh is the largest city in Saudi Arabia.","on_screen":"Mount Everest is the highest mountain in the world. / My grandfather is the oldest person in our family. / Riyadh is the largest city in Saudi Arabia.","visual":"Each example appears on a card with a small picture; the target part bounces once and turns green."},{"time":"02:15–02:45","narration":"Be careful! Some learners say: “Burj Khalifa is tallest building.” That’s not right. We say: “The Burj Khalifa is the tallest building.” Use the before a superlative.","on_screen":"✗ Burj Khalifa is tallest building.   ✓ The Burj Khalifa is the tallest building.","visual":"A red cross stamps the wrong sentence; it slides away and the correct sentence appears with a green tick."},{"time":"02:45–03:05","narration":"Quick check: How many things do we compare with \"the fastest\"? … Think! … Three or more. Great job! Now you can say: I can say \"the tallest building in the world\".","on_screen":"Quick check ✔  |  I can: I can say \"the tallest building in the world\".","visual":"Three-second pause with a countdown ring; Zaki gives a wing \"thumbs up\" and confetti in the programme colours."}],"captions_ar":["مرحبًا، أنا زكي! درس اليوم: superlative adjectives (the -est / the most …; the best, the worst).","استمع وانتبه إلى الكلمات الملوّنة بالأخضر.","نستخدم صيغة التفضيل لمقارنة شيء واحد بكل الأشياء الأخرى في مجموعة: the fastest (الأسرع).","لاحظ الأمثلة: الجزء الملوّن هو القاعدة.","انتبه! الخطأ: Burj Khalifa is tallest building. — الصحيح: The Burj Khalifa is the tallest building.","سؤال سريع… فكّر ثم أجب. أحسنت! الآن تستطيع: أستطيع أن أقول the tallest building in the world."]},"texts":[{"type":"reading","title":"Amazing Record Facts","body":"Omar loves amazing facts, so he made a poster for his class.\nThe tallest building in the world is the Burj Khalifa in Dubai. It is 828 meters high!\nThe highest fountain in the world is King Fahd's Fountain in Jeddah. Its water goes up to 312 meters.\nThe blue whale is the biggest animal on Earth, and the cheetah is the fastest animal on land.\nThe Rub' al Khali is the largest sand desert in the world.\n\"Which fact is the most interesting?\" asked Mr. Khalid.\n\"The fountain!\" said Omar. \"It's the best fact because it's from our country!\"","word_count":100,"audio_id":"AUD-GV-L04-U1-LS1-T1"}],"activities":[{"id":"GV-L04-U1-LS1-A1","type":"mcq","instructions":"Controlled practice: Choose the correct answer.","items":[{"q":"The cheetah is ___ animal on land.","options":["the fastest","faster","fastest","the most fast"],"answer":"the fastest","explanation":"Short adjective → the + -est.","explanation_ar":"الصفة القصيرة ← the + est."},{"q":"This is ___ book in the library.","options":["more interesting","the most interesting","most interestinger","the interestingest"],"answer":"the most interesting","explanation":"Long adjective → the most + adjective.","explanation_ar":"الصفة الطويلة ← the most."},{"q":"Kabsa is ___ dish in the restaurant!","options":["best of","the goodest","the better","the best"],"answer":"the best","explanation":"good → the best; bad → the worst.","explanation_ar":"صيغ شاذة."},{"q":"Faisal is the tallest boy ___ our class.","options":["of","in","on","at"],"answer":"in","explanation":"in + place or group (in the world, in my class).","explanation_ar":"in مع المكان أو المجموعة."},{"q":"The Pacific is ___ ocean in the world.","options":["the deepest","deepest","the most deep","the deeper"],"answer":"the deepest","explanation":"Always use the before a superlative.","explanation_ar":"لا بد من the."},{"q":"Yesterday was ___ day of my life!","options":["the baddest","worst of","the worst","the worse"],"answer":"the worst","explanation":"good → the best; bad → the worst.","explanation_ar":"صيغ شاذة."}]},{"id":"GV-L04-U1-LS1-B1","type":"gap_fill","instructions":"Guided practice: Write the superlative. Word bank: the youngest, the highest, the most beautiful","items":[{"q":"Jabal Sawda is ______ (high) mountain in Saudi Arabia.","options":[],"answer":"the highest","explanation":"Short adjective → the + -est.","explanation_ar":"الصفة القصيرة ← the + est."},{"q":"This is ______ (beautiful) beach on the Red Sea.","options":[],"answer":"the most beautiful","explanation":"Long adjective → the most + adjective.","explanation_ar":"الصفة الطويلة ← the most."},{"q":"Lina is ______ (young) girl in her family.","options":[],"answer":"the youngest","explanation":"Short adjective → the + -est.","explanation_ar":"الصفة القصيرة ← the + est."}]},{"id":"GV-L04-U1-LS1-B2","type":"open","instructions":"Guided practice: Make sentences with the superlative.","items":[{"q":"Riyadh / large / city in Saudi Arabia  (superlative)","options":[],"answer":"Riyadh is the largest city in Saudi Arabia.","explanation":"Short adjective → the + -est.","explanation_ar":"الصفة القصيرة ← the + est."},{"q":"chess / difficult / game I know  (superlative)","options":[],"answer":"Chess is the most difficult game I know.","explanation":"Long adjective → the most + adjective.","explanation_ar":"الصفة الطويلة ← the most."},{"q":"my mom / good / cook in the family  (superlative)","options":[],"answer":"My mom is the best cook in the family.","explanation":"good → the best; bad → the worst.","explanation_ar":"صيغ شاذة."}]},{"id":"GV-L04-U1-LS1-C1","type":"open","instructions":"Freer practice: Write about your records.","items":[{"q":"The tallest person in my family is ___.","options":[],"answer":"The tallest person in my family is my uncle Saad.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses superlative adjectives (the -est / the most …; the best, the worst) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"The most interesting subject for me is ___.","options":[],"answer":"The most interesting subject for me is science.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses superlative adjectives (the -est / the most …; the best, the worst) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"The best day of the week is ___.","options":[],"answer":"The best day of the week is Friday.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses superlative adjectives (the -est / the most …; the best, the worst) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"The oldest building in my town is ___.","options":[],"answer":"The oldest building in my town is the old fort.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses superlative adjectives (the -est / the most …; the best, the worst) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"The most delicious food I know is ___.","options":[],"answer":"The most delicious food I know is my grandma's jareesh.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses superlative adjectives (the -est / the most …; the best, the worst) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."}]},{"id":"GV-L04-U1-LS1-D1","type":"open","instructions":"Production: Class record book.","items":[{"q":"Write 4 class records with superlatives.","options":[],"answer":"Turki is the fastest runner. Hamad is the best artist. Ziyad is the tallest. Nawaf has the longest name.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses superlative adjectives (the -est / the most …; the best, the worst) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Write 2 facts about the world with superlatives.","options":[],"answer":"The Sahara is the largest hot desert. Antarctica is the coldest place on Earth.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses superlative adjectives (the -est / the most …; the best, the worst) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Ask a partner \"What's the most exciting place you've visited?\" Write his answer.","options":[],"answer":"The most exciting place he visited is Al-Ula.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses superlative adjectives (the -est / the most …; the best, the worst) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."}]}],"game":{"name":"Grammar Hot Seat","mechanic":"timed_quiz","rules":["One student from each team sits in the hot seat facing the class.","The teacher shows a cue card behind the student; the team gives a clue using superlative adjectives (the -est / the most …; the best, the worst) without saying the word.","The student in the hot seat guesses the cue word within 30 seconds.","Teams score 1 point for a correct guess and 1 point for a correct clue sentence. Rotate seats."],"data":[{"label":"the tallest"},{"label":"the fastest"},{"label":"the biggest"},{"label":"the most famous"},{"label":"the best"},{"label":"the worst"},{"label":"the longest"},{"label":"the most dangerous"}]},"exit_quiz":[{"q":"The blue whale is ___ animal on Earth.","options":["the bigest","the most big","the biggest","bigger"],"answer":"the biggest","explanation":"Short adjective → the + -est.","explanation_ar":"الصفة القصيرة ← the + est."},{"q":"Gold is ___ of the three metals.","options":["the more expensive","the expensivest","the most expensive","most expensive"],"answer":"the most expensive","explanation":"Long adjective → the most + adjective.","explanation_ar":"الصفة الطويلة ← the most."},{"q":"This is ___ pizza in town!","options":["the best","the goodest","the better","best of all the"],"answer":"the best","explanation":"good → the best; bad → the worst.","explanation_ar":"صيغ شاذة."},{"q":"","options":["Riyadh is the biggest city of Saudi Arabia.","Riyadh is the most big city in Saudi Arabia.","Riyadh is biggest city in Saudi Arabia.","Riyadh is the biggest city in Saudi Arabia."],"answer":"Riyadh is the biggest city in Saudi Arabia.","explanation":"Always use the before a superlative.","explanation_ar":"لا بد من the."},{"q":"Antarctica is ___ continent.","options":["coldest of","the most cold","colder","the coldest"],"answer":"the coldest","explanation":"Short adjective → the + -est.","explanation_ar":"الصفة القصيرة ← the + est."},{"q":"","options":["My little brother is funniest person in our house.","My little brother is the funniest person in our house.","My little brother is the funnier person in our house.","My little brother is the most funny person in our house."],"answer":"My little brother is the funniest person in our house.","explanation":"Short adjective → the + -est.","explanation_ar":"الصفة القصيرة ← the + est."},{"q":"It was ___ traffic jam of the year.","options":["the baddest","the worst","worst of","the worse"],"answer":"the worst","explanation":"good → the best; bad → the worst.","explanation_ar":"صيغ شاذة."},{"q":"The Nile is one of ___ rivers in the world.","options":["the longest","the most long","longest of","longer"],"answer":"the longest","explanation":"Short adjective → the + -est.","explanation_ar":"الصفة القصيرة ← the + est."},{"q":"","options":["She is most famous singer in the country.","She is the most famous singer in the country.","She is the more famous singer in the country.","She is the famousest singer in the country."],"answer":"She is the most famous singer in the country.","explanation":"Long adjective → the most + adjective.","explanation_ar":"الصفة الطويلة ← the most."},{"q":"Who is the oldest person ___ your family?","options":["on","at","of","in"],"answer":"in","explanation":"in + place or group (in the world, in my class).","explanation_ar":"in مع المكان أو المجموعة."}],"images":[{"id":"GV-L04-U1-LS1-IMG01","prompt":"Omar presenting a \"World Records\" poster to his class with pictures of the Burj Khalifa, King Fahd's Fountain, a blue whale and a cheetah. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Landscape 16:9.","alt":"Omar presenting a \"World Records\" poster to his class with pictures of the Burj Khalifa, King Fahd's Fountain, a blue whale and a cheetah"},{"id":"GV-L04-U1-LS1-IMG02","prompt":"clean background panel for a grammar box about superlative adjectives (the -est / the most …; the best, the worst), with Zaki the Falcon pointing at a blank board on the right; leave large empty space for text overlay. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"clean background panel for a grammar box about superlative adjectives (the -est / the most …"},{"id":"GV-L04-U1-LS1-W01","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows record (the best result that anyone has ever had); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing record: the best result that anyone has ever had"},{"id":"GV-L04-U1-LS1-W02","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows champion (a person or team that wins a competition); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing champion: a person or team that wins a competition"},{"id":"GV-L04-U1-LS1-W03","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows height (how tall or high something is); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing height: how tall or high something is"},{"id":"GV-L04-U1-LS1-W04","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows length (how long something is); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing length: how long something is"},{"id":"GV-L04-U1-LS1-G01","prompt":"Card-back and board design for the classroom game “Grammar Hot Seat”: Zaki the Falcon icon in the centre, Leaf Green border with navy stars. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image. Portrait 2:3.","alt":"Game card design for Grammar Hot Seat"}],"audio":[{"id":"AUD-GV-L04-U1-LS1-W01","script":"record. record. She broke the school record for running.","voice":"en-US, warm female or male teacher voice","speed":"0.9"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L04-U1-LS1-W02","script":"champion. champion. The champion lifted the gold cup.","voice":"en-US, warm female or male teacher voice","speed":"0.9"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L04-U1-LS1-W03","script":"height. height. The height of the tower is 828 meters.","voice":"en-US, warm female or male teacher voice","speed":"0.9"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L04-U1-LS1-W04","script":"length. length. The length of the river is 6,650 kilometers.","voice":"en-US, warm female or male teacher voice","speed":"0.9"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L04-U1-LS1-T1","script":"Omar loves amazing facts, so he made a poster for his class. The tallest building in the world is the Burj Khalifa in Dubai. It is 828 meters high! The highest fountain in the world is King Fahd's Fountain in Jeddah. Its water goes up to 312 meters. The blue whale is the biggest animal on Earth, and the cheetah is the fastest animal on land. The Rub' al Khali is the largest sand desert in the world. \"Which fact is the most interesting?\" asked Mr. Khalid. \"The fountain!\" said Omar. \"It's the best fact because it's from our country!\"","voice":"en-US, warm female or male teacher voice","speed":"0.9"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L04-U1-LS1-VID","script":"Hi, I’m Zaki! Today’s lesson is “The Tallest Building in the World: Superlative Adjectives”. Let’s learn superlative adjectives (the -est / the most …; the best, the worst) together. Listen to the start of “Amazing Record Facts”: Omar loves amazing facts, so he made a poster for his class. The tallest building in the world is the Burj Khalifa in Dubai. It is 828 meters high! The highest fountain in the world is King Fahd's Fountain in Jeddah. Look at the green words. We use superlatives to compare one thing with all the others in a group (three or more): The cheetah is the fastest animal on land. Short adjectives: the + adjective + -est: tall → the tallest. Long adjectives: the most + adjective: interesting → the most interesting. Here are some examples. Mount Everest is the highest mountain in the world. My grandfather is the oldest person in our family. Riyadh is the largest city in Saudi Arabia. Be careful! Some learners say: “Burj Khalifa is tallest building.” That’s not right. We say: “The Burj Khalifa is the tallest building.” Use the before a superlative. Quick check: How many things do we compare with \"the fastest\"? … Think! … Three or more. Great job! Now you can say: I can say \"the tallest building in the world\".","voice":"en-US, Zaki the Falcon narrator voice (bright, friendly)","speed":"0.9"}]},{"id":"GV-L04-U1-LS2","title":"Bigger or the Biggest? Comparatives vs Superlatives","objectives":["Students will be able to choose between a comparative (two things) and a superlative (three or more).","Students will be able to use the least and one of the … + plural noun.","I can choose \"bigger than\" or \"the biggest\".","I can say \"one of the tallest towers\" and \"the least expensive\"."],"objectives_ar":["سيتمكن الطلاب من الاختيار بين صيغة المقارنة (لشيئين) وصيغة التفضيل (لثلاثة أو أكثر).","سيتمكن الطلاب من استخدام the least وone of the + جمع.","أستطيع أن أختار بين bigger than وthe biggest.","أستطيع أن أقول one of the tallest towers وthe least expensive."],"vocabulary":[{"word":"weight","pos":"noun","ipa":"/weɪt/","definition":"how heavy something is","arabic":"وزن","example":"The weight of a blue whale is about 150 tons.","image_id":"GV-L04-U1-LS2-W01","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L04-U1-LS2-W01"},{"word":"speed","pos":"noun","ipa":"/spid/","definition":"how fast something moves","arabic":"سرعة","example":"A cheetah can reach a speed of 110 kilometers per hour.","image_id":"GV-L04-U1-LS2-W02","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L04-U1-LS2-W02"},{"word":"meter","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈmitɚ/","definition":"a measure of length; 100 centimeters","arabic":"متر","example":"The pool is 50 meters long.","image_id":"GV-L04-U1-LS2-W03","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L04-U1-LS2-W03"},{"word":"kilometer","pos":"noun","ipa":"/kəˈlɑmətɚ/","definition":"a measure of distance; 1,000 meters","arabic":"كيلومتر","example":"My school is two kilometers from home.","image_id":"GV-L04-U1-LS2-W04","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L04-U1-LS2-W04"}],"explanation":{"text":"Use a comparative for two things: The bike is faster than the scooter. Use a superlative for three or more: The car is the fastest of the three.\nthe least is the opposite of the most: This is the least expensive phone (= the cheapest).\none of the + superlative + plural noun: The Burj Khalifa is one of the most famous buildings in the world.","examples":["My brother is taller than me, but my dad is the tallest in the family.","This is the least difficult question on the test.","The Kaaba is one of the most important places in the world.","The red shoes are more comfortable than the black ones.","The blue shoes are the most comfortable of all.","Football is one of the most popular sports in Saudi Arabia.","Which is the least noisy room in the house?","Of the three cities, Jeddah is the busiest."],"common_errors":["✗ She is the taller girl in the class. → ✓ She is the tallest girl in the class. (A whole class (3+) → superlative.)","✗ My bike is the fastest than yours. → ✓ My bike is faster than yours. (Two things → comparative + than.)","✗ It's one of the best restaurant. → ✓ It's one of the best restaurants. (one of the + plural noun.)","✗ This is the less expensive of all. → ✓ This is the least expensive of all. (3+ → the least.)"],"arabic":"المقارنة (comparative) لشيئين مع than، والتفضيل (superlative) لثلاثة أو أكثر مع the.\nthe least عكس the most: the least expensive = الأرخص (الأقل سعرًا).\none of the + صيغة التفضيل + اسم جمع: one of the best players."},"video":{"script":[{"time":"00:00–00:20","narration":"Hi, I’m Zaki! Today’s lesson is “Bigger or the Biggest? Comparatives vs Superlatives”. Let’s learn comparatives vs superlatives; the most / the least; one of the + superlative + plural noun together.","on_screen":"GV-L04-U1-LS2 | Bigger or the Biggest? Comparatives vs Superlatives","visual":"Zaki the Falcon flies in over the Leaf Green title card and lands next to the lesson title; soft chime."},{"time":"00:20–00:45","narration":"Remember these patterns: Abha is cooler than Riyadh. • Abha is the coolest city of the three. • It's one of the coolest cities in Saudi Arabia. This bag isn't the cheapest. • It isn't the least comfortable chair. Which is the most popular sport in your school? • Is it one of the biggest malls in Riyadh?","on_screen":"Abha is cooler than Riyadh. • Abha is the coolest city of the three. • It's one of the coolest cities in Saudi Arabia. | This bag isn't the cheapest. • It isn't the least comfortable chair. | Which is the most popular sport in your school? • Is it one of the biggest malls in Riyadh?","visual":"Pattern strips slide in from the left; the key words are highlighted in Leaf Green."},{"time":"00:45–01:30","narration":"Use a comparative for two things: The bike is faster than the scooter. Use a superlative for three or more: The car is the fastest of the three. the least is the opposite of the most: This is the least expensive phone (= the cheapest).","on_screen":"comparatives vs superlatives; the most / the least; one of the + superlative + plural noun","visual":"Grammar box builds line by line (form → meaning → use); Zaki points to each line."},{"time":"01:30–02:15","narration":"Here are some examples. My brother is taller than me, but my dad is the tallest in the family. This is the least difficult question on the test. The Kaaba is one of the most important places in the world.","on_screen":"My brother is taller than me, but my dad is the tallest in the family. / This is the least difficult question on the test. / The Kaaba is one of the most important places in the world.","visual":"Each example appears on a card with a small picture; the target part bounces once and turns green."},{"time":"02:15–02:45","narration":"Be careful! Some learners say: “She is the taller girl in the class.” That’s not right. We say: “She is the tallest girl in the class.” A whole class (3+) → superlative.","on_screen":"✗ She is the taller girl in the class.   ✓ She is the tallest girl in the class.","visual":"A red cross stamps the wrong sentence; it slides away and the correct sentence appears with a green tick."},{"time":"02:45–03:05","narration":"Quick check: \"Faisal is ___ than Saad.\" Two people or more? Which form? … Think! … Two – comparative: taller than. Great job! Now you can say: I can choose \"bigger than\" or \"the biggest\".","on_screen":"Quick check ✔  |  I can: I can choose \"bigger than\" or \"the biggest\".","visual":"Three-second pause with a countdown ring; Zaki gives a wing \"thumbs up\" and confetti in the programme colours."}],"captions_ar":["مرحبًا، أنا زكي! درس اليوم: comparatives vs superlatives; the most / the least; one of the + superlative + plural noun.","استمع وانتبه إلى الكلمات الملوّنة بالأخضر.","المقارنة (comparative) لشيئين مع than، والتفضيل (superlative) لثلاثة أو أكثر مع the.","لاحظ الأمثلة: الجزء الملوّن هو القاعدة.","انتبه! الخطأ: She is the taller girl in the class. — الصحيح: She is the tallest girl in the class.","سؤال سريع… فكّر ثم أجب. أحسنت! الآن تستطيع: أستطيع أن أختار بين bigger than وthe biggest."]},"texts":[],"activities":[{"id":"GV-L04-U1-LS2-A1","type":"mcq","instructions":"Controlled practice: Choose the correct answer.","items":[{"q":"My phone is ___ than my sister's phone.","options":["the newest","the newer","newest","newer"],"answer":"newer","explanation":"Two things → comparative + than.","explanation_ar":"شيئان ← المقارنة + than."},{"q":"Of the three boys, Hamad is ___.","options":["stronger","the strongest","strongest than","the stronger"],"answer":"the strongest","explanation":"Three or more → the + superlative.","explanation_ar":"ثلاثة أو أكثر ← صيغة التفضيل."},{"q":"This is ___ expensive watch in the shop. It's very cheap.","options":["lesser","less","the most","the least"],"answer":"the least","explanation":"the least = the smallest amount (opposite of the most).","explanation_ar":"the least عكس the most."},{"q":"Jeddah is one of the biggest ___ in Saudi Arabia.","options":["citys","the city","cities","city"],"answer":"cities","explanation":"one of the + superlative + plural noun.","explanation_ar":"one of the + جمع."},{"q":"A car is ___ than a bicycle.","options":["faster","the faster","the fastest","fastest"],"answer":"faster","explanation":"Two things → comparative + than.","explanation_ar":"شيئان ← المقارنة + than."},{"q":"Of all the subjects, math is ___ for me.","options":["easiest than","easier","the easiest","the easier"],"answer":"the easiest","explanation":"Three or more → the + superlative.","explanation_ar":"ثلاثة أو أكثر ← صيغة التفضيل."}]},{"id":"GV-L04-U1-LS2-B1","type":"gap_fill","instructions":"Guided practice: Comparative or superlative? Write the correct form. Word bank: bigger, the least, the biggest","items":[{"q":"Riyadh is ______ (big) than Taif.","options":[],"answer":"bigger","explanation":"Two things → comparative + than.","explanation_ar":"شيئان ← المقارنة + than."},{"q":"Riyadh is ______ (big) city in Saudi Arabia.","options":[],"answer":"the biggest","explanation":"Three or more → the + superlative.","explanation_ar":"ثلاثة أو أكثر ← صيغة التفضيل."},{"q":"This chair is ______ (comfortable) comfortable of all. Don't sit on it!","options":[],"answer":"the least","explanation":"the least = the smallest amount (opposite of the most).","explanation_ar":"the least عكس the most."}]},{"id":"GV-L04-U1-LS2-B2","type":"open","instructions":"Guided practice: Write with one of the.","items":[{"q":"Al-Ula / beautiful / place in Saudi Arabia  (one of the)","options":[],"answer":"Al-Ula is one of the most beautiful places in Saudi Arabia.","explanation":"one of the + superlative + plural noun.","explanation_ar":"one of the + جمع."},{"q":"Ziyad / good / player in our team  (one of the)","options":[],"answer":"Ziyad is one of the best players in our team.","explanation":"one of the + superlative + plural noun.","explanation_ar":"one of the + جمع."},{"q":"the cheetah / fast / animal in the world  (one of the)","options":[],"answer":"The cheetah is one of the fastest animals in the world.","explanation":"one of the + superlative + plural noun.","explanation_ar":"one of the + جمع."}]},{"id":"GV-L04-U1-LS2-C1","type":"open","instructions":"Freer practice: Compare things you know.","items":[{"q":"My ___ is older than my ___.","options":[],"answer":"My grandpa is older than my grandma.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses comparatives vs superlatives; the most / the least; one of the + superlative + plural noun correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"The most popular game in my class is ___.","options":[],"answer":"The most popular game in my class is football.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses comparatives vs superlatives; the most / the least; one of the + superlative + plural noun correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"The least interesting TV program for me is ___.","options":[],"answer":"The least interesting TV program for me is the news.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses comparatives vs superlatives; the most / the least; one of the + superlative + plural noun correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"___ is one of the best places in my town.","options":[],"answer":"The new park is one of the best places in my town.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses comparatives vs superlatives; the most / the least; one of the + superlative + plural noun correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Of my three best friends, ___ is the funniest.","options":[],"answer":"Of my three best friends, Turki is the funniest.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses comparatives vs superlatives; the most / the least; one of the + superlative + plural noun correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."}]},{"id":"GV-L04-U1-LS2-D1","type":"open","instructions":"Production: Shopping decisions.","items":[{"q":"Compare three phones (cheap, middle, expensive). Write 3 sentences.","options":[],"answer":"Phone A is the cheapest. Phone B is more expensive than Phone A. Phone C is the most expensive.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses comparatives vs superlatives; the most / the least; one of the + superlative + plural noun correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Write which one you would buy and why with the least or the most.","options":[],"answer":"I'd buy Phone B because it isn't the most expensive, but it's the best camera.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses comparatives vs superlatives; the most / the least; one of the + superlative + plural noun correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Write one sentence with one of the about your country.","options":[],"answer":"Jeddah is one of the oldest cities on the Red Sea.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses comparatives vs superlatives; the most / the least; one of the + superlative + plural noun correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."}]}],"game":{"name":"Sentence Builder Race","mechanic":"sentence_builder","rules":["Each team receives the same tile set.","In 5 minutes, build as many different correct sentences as possible using comparatives vs superlatives; the most / the least; one of the + superlative + plural noun.","Write each sentence on the team sheet.","Swap sheets with another team to check. One point per correct sentence; no points for repeats."],"data":[{"cue":"the cheetah / fast / land animal"},{"cue":"the Burj Khalifa / tall / building"},{"cue":"the blue whale / big / animal"},{"cue":"Mount Everest / high / mountain"},{"cue":"the Rub' al Khali / large / sand desert"},{"cue":"gold / expensive / of the three"},{"cue":"my grandma / good / cook in the family"},{"cue":"the Pacific / deep / ocean"},{"cue":"this / bad / day of the week"}]},"exit_quiz":[{"q":"Sara is ___ than her sister.","options":["the oldest","oldest","older","the older"],"answer":"older","explanation":"Two things → comparative + than.","explanation_ar":"شيئان ← المقارنة + than."},{"q":"This is ___ exciting ride in the park!","options":["the most","the more","more","most"],"answer":"the most","explanation":"Three or more → the + superlative.","explanation_ar":"ثلاثة أو أكثر ← صيغة التفضيل."},{"q":"Which is ___ planet, Mercury, Venus or Mars?","options":["smaller","smallest than","the most small","the smallest"],"answer":"the smallest","explanation":"Three or more → the + superlative.","explanation_ar":"ثلاثة أو أكثر ← صيغة التفضيل."},{"q":"","options":["It's one of the oldest mosques in the city.","It's one of oldest mosques in the city.","It's one of the oldest mosque in the city.","It's one the oldest mosques in the city."],"answer":"It's one of the oldest mosques in the city.","explanation":"one of the + superlative + plural noun.","explanation_ar":"one of the + جمع."},{"q":"","options":["This is the least expensive hotel in town.","This is the less expensive hotel in town.","This is least expensive hotel in town.","This is the leastest expensive hotel in town."],"answer":"This is the least expensive hotel in town.","explanation":"the least = the smallest amount (opposite of the most).","explanation_ar":"the least عكس the most."},{"q":"","options":["My bag is heavyer than your bag.","My bag is more heavy than your bag.","My bag is heavier than your bag.","My bag is the heaviest than your bag."],"answer":"My bag is heavier than your bag.","explanation":"Two things → comparative + than.","explanation_ar":"شيئان ← المقارنة + than."},{"q":"","options":["Of the four seasons, spring is the most nice.","Of the four seasons, spring is the nicest.","Of the four seasons, spring is nicest than.","Of the four seasons, spring is nicer."],"answer":"Of the four seasons, spring is the nicest.","explanation":"Three or more → the + superlative.","explanation_ar":"ثلاثة أو أكثر ← صيغة التفضيل."},{"q":"Football is one of the most popular ___ in the world.","options":["the sport","sport","sport's","sports"],"answer":"sports","explanation":"one of the + superlative + plural noun.","explanation_ar":"one of the + جمع."},{"q":"The red car is fast, the blue car is faster, and the white car is ___.","options":["fastest than","faster","the fastest","the faster"],"answer":"the fastest","explanation":"Three or more → the + superlative.","explanation_ar":"ثلاثة أو أكثر ← صيغة التفضيل."},{"q":"Which word is the opposite of \"the most\"?","options":["the less","the least","the little","the lest"],"answer":"the least","explanation":"the least = the smallest amount (opposite of the most).","explanation_ar":"the least عكس the most."}],"images":[{"id":"GV-L04-U1-LS2-IMG01","prompt":"Three sneakers on a shop shelf with price tags (SR 90, SR 150, SR 300), Yusuf comparing them while his father points at the cheapest. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Landscape 16:9.","alt":"Three sneakers on a shop shelf with price tags (SR 90, SR 150, SR 300), Yusuf comparing them while his father points at the cheapest"},{"id":"GV-L04-U1-LS2-IMG02","prompt":"two-panel visual contrasting correct and incorrect use of comparatives vs superlatives; the most / the least; one of the + superlative + plural noun: a green tick panel and a soft red cross panel with simple objects from the theme “Record Breakers”; empty space for text overlay. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"two-panel visual contrasting correct and incorrect use of comparatives vs superlatives"},{"id":"GV-L04-U1-LS2-W01","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows weight (how heavy something is); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing weight: how heavy something is"},{"id":"GV-L04-U1-LS2-W02","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows speed (how fast something moves); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing speed: how fast something moves"},{"id":"GV-L04-U1-LS2-W03","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows meter (a measure of length; 100 centimeters); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing meter: a measure of length; 100 centimeters"},{"id":"GV-L04-U1-LS2-W04","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows kilometer (a measure of distance; 1,000 meters); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing kilometer: a measure of distance; 1,000 meters"},{"id":"GV-L04-U1-LS2-G01","prompt":"Card-back and board design for the classroom game “Sentence Builder Race”: Zaki the Falcon icon in the centre, Leaf Green border with navy stars. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image. Portrait 2:3.","alt":"Game card design for Sentence Builder Race"}],"audio":[{"id":"AUD-GV-L04-U1-LS2-W01","script":"weight. weight. The weight of a blue whale is about 150 tons.","voice":"en-US, warm female or male teacher voice","speed":"0.9"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L04-U1-LS2-W02","script":"speed. speed. A cheetah can reach a speed of 110 kilometers per hour.","voice":"en-US, warm female or male teacher voice","speed":"0.9"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L04-U1-LS2-W03","script":"meter. meter. The pool is 50 meters long.","voice":"en-US, warm female or male teacher voice","speed":"0.9"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L04-U1-LS2-W04","script":"kilometer. kilometer. My school is two kilometers from home.","voice":"en-US, warm female or male teacher voice","speed":"0.9"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L04-U1-LS2-VID","script":"Hi, I’m Zaki! Today’s lesson is “Bigger or the Biggest? Comparatives vs Superlatives”. Let’s learn comparatives vs superlatives; the most / the least; one of the + superlative + plural noun together. Remember these patterns: Abha is cooler than Riyadh. • Abha is the coolest city of the three. • It's one of the coolest cities in Saudi Arabia. This bag isn't the cheapest. • It isn't the least comfortable chair. Which is the most popular sport in your school? • Is it one of the biggest malls in Riyadh? Use a comparative for two things: The bike is faster than the scooter. Use a superlative for three or more: The car is the fastest of the three. the least is the opposite of the most: This is the least expensive phone (= the cheapest). Here are some examples. My brother is taller than me, but my dad is the tallest in the family. This is the least difficult question on the test. The Kaaba is one of the most important places in the world. Be careful! Some learners say: “She is the taller girl in the class.” That’s not right. We say: “She is the tallest girl in the class.” A whole class (3+) → superlative. Quick check: \"Faisal is ___ than Saad.\" Two people or more? Which form? … Think! … Two – comparative: taller than. Great job! Now you can say: I can choose \"bigger than\" or \"the biggest\".","voice":"en-US, Zaki the Falcon narrator voice (bright, friendly)","speed":"0.9"}]},{"id":"GV-L04-U1-LS3","title":"Height, Length, Speed: Measurement Words and Word Families","objectives":["Students will be able to use measurement nouns (height, length, width, depth, weight, speed).","Students will be able to build word families from adjectives (wide → width → widen).","I can say \"The height of the tower is 828 meters.\"","I can change \"long\" to \"length\" and \"strong\" to \"strength\"."],"objectives_ar":["سيتمكن الطلاب من استخدام أسماء القياس (height وlength وwidth وdepth وweight وspeed).","سيتمكن الطلاب من تكوين عائلات الكلمات من الصفات (wide → width → widen).","أستطيع أن أقول The height of the tower is 828 meters.","أستطيع أن أحوّل long إلى length وstrong إلى strength."],"vocabulary":[{"word":"kilogram","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈkɪləˌɡræm/","definition":"a measure of weight; 1,000 grams","arabic":"كيلوغرام","example":"This watermelon weighs five kilograms.","image_id":"GV-L04-U1-LS3-W01","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L04-U1-LS3-W01"},{"word":"tower","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈtaʊɚ/","definition":"a very tall, narrow building","arabic":"برج","example":"The TV tower in Riyadh is very tall.","image_id":"GV-L04-U1-LS3-W02","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L04-U1-LS3-W02"},{"word":"fountain","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈfaʊntən/","definition":"a structure that sends water up into the air","arabic":"نافورة","example":"The fountain in the park lights up at night.","image_id":"GV-L04-U1-LS3-W03","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L04-U1-LS3-W03"},{"word":"giant","pos":"adjective","ipa":"/ˈdʒaɪənt/","definition":"very, very big","arabic":"عملاق","example":"A giant tortoise can live for 150 years.","image_id":"GV-L04-U1-LS3-W04","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L04-U1-LS3-W04"},{"word":"amazing","pos":"adjective","ipa":"/əˈmeɪzɪŋ/","definition":"very surprising and wonderful","arabic":"مذهل","example":"The view from the top was amazing.","image_id":"GV-L04-U1-LS3-W05","audio_id":"AUD-GV-L04-U1-LS3-W05"}],"explanation":{"text":"Many measurement nouns come from adjectives: high → height, long → length, wide → width, deep → depth, strong → strength, heavy → weight, fast → speed.\nUse the noun with the … of: The length of the river is 6,650 kilometers. Use the adjective with be: The river is 6,650 kilometers long.\nUnits: meters (m) and kilometers (km) for length, height and distance; kilograms (kg) and tons for weight; kilometers per hour (km/h) for speed.\nWord families: high: height (n), highly (adv) | long: length (n), lengthen (v) | wide: width (n), widen (v) | deep: depth (n), deepen (v) | strong: strength (n), strengthen (v)\nCollocations/phrases: break a record • set a record • hold a record • become the champion • win first place","examples":["The height of Jabal Sawda is about 3,000 meters.","The road is 20 meters wide.","The depth of the pool is two meters.","An elephant's weight can be six tons.","The runner broke the record for 100 meters.","The champion trained every day.","A falcon can dive at a speed of 300 kilometers per hour.","The workers widened the old road."],"common_errors":["✗ The long of the river is 50 km. → ✓ The length of the river is 50 km. (Use the noun length after the … of.)","✗ The tower is 300 meters height. → ✓ The tower is 300 meters high. (After the number, use the adjective.)","✗ He made a new record. → ✓ He set / broke a new record. (set/break a record.)","✗ The heavy of the bag is 5 kg. → ✓ The weight of the bag is 5 kg. (heavy → weight.)"],"arabic":"كثير من أسماء القياس تأتي من الصفات: high → height (ارتفاع)، long → length (طول)، wide → width (عرض)، deep → depth (عمق).\nنقول The length of the river… (الاسم) أو The river is 50 km long (الصفة).\nنقول break a record (يحطم رقمًا قياسيًا) وset a record (يسجّل رقمًا قياسيًا)."},"video":{"script":[{"time":"00:00–00:20","narration":"Hi, I’m Zaki! Today’s lesson is “Height, Length, Speed: Measurement Words and Word Families”. Let’s learn measurement nouns from adjectives (high → height, long → length, strong → strength); record words; units together.","on_screen":"GV-L04-U1-LS3 | Height, Length, Speed: Measurement Words and Word Families","visual":"Zaki the Falcon flies in over the Leaf Green title card and lands next to the lesson title; soft chime."},{"time":"00:20–00:45","narration":"Meet some new words. kilogram: a measure of weight; 1,000 grams. tower: a very tall, narrow building. fountain: a structure that sends water up into the air.","on_screen":"kilogram | tower | fountain","visual":"Each word card flips over to show its picture (vocabulary image briefs) and Arabic meaning."},{"time":"00:45–01:30","narration":"Many measurement nouns come from adjectives: high → height, long → length, wide → width, deep → depth, strong → strength, heavy → weight, fast → speed. Use the noun with the … of: The length of the river is 6,650 kilometers. Use the adjective with be: The river is 6,650 kilometers long.","on_screen":"measurement nouns from adjectives (high → height, long → length, strong → strength); record words; units","visual":"Grammar box builds line by line (form → meaning → use); Zaki points to each line."},{"time":"01:30–02:15","narration":"Here are some examples. The height of Jabal Sawda is about 3,000 meters. The road is 20 meters wide. The depth of the pool is two meters.","on_screen":"The height of Jabal Sawda is about 3,000 meters. / The road is 20 meters wide. / The depth of the pool is two meters.","visual":"Each example appears on a card with a small picture; the target part bounces once and turns green."},{"time":"02:15–02:45","narration":"Be careful! Some learners say: “The long of the river is 50 km.” That’s not right. We say: “The length of the river is 50 km.” Use the noun length after the … of.","on_screen":"✗ The long of the river is 50 km.   ✓ The length of the river is 50 km.","visual":"A red cross stamps the wrong sentence; it slides away and the correct sentence appears with a green tick."},{"time":"02:45–03:05","narration":"Quick check: What is the noun from \"strong\"? … Think! … *strength*. Great job! Now you can say: I can say \"The height of the tower is 828 meters.\"","on_screen":"Quick check ✔  |  I can: I can say \"The height of the tower is 828 meters.\"","visual":"Three-second pause with a countdown ring; Zaki gives a wing \"thumbs up\" and confetti in the programme colours."}],"captions_ar":["مرحبًا، أنا زكي! درس اليوم: measurement nouns from adjectives (high → height, long → length, strong → strength); record words; units.","استمع وانتبه إلى الكلمات الملوّنة بالأخضر.","كثير من أسماء القياس تأتي من الصفات: high → height (ارتفاع)، long → length (طول)، wide → width (عرض)، deep → depth (عمق).","لاحظ الأمثلة: الجزء الملوّن هو القاعدة.","انتبه! الخطأ: The long of the river is 50 km. — الصحيح: The length of the river is 50 km.","سؤال سريع… فكّر ثم أجب. أحسنت! الآن تستطيع: أستطيع أن أقول The height of the tower is 828 meters."]},"texts":[],"activities":[{"id":"GV-L04-U1-LS3-A1","type":"mcq","instructions":"Controlled practice: Choose the correct word.","items":[{"q":"The ___ of the tower is 300 meters.","options":["height","highly","heighten","high"],"answer":"height","explanation":"Use the measurement noun after \"the … of\".","explanation_ar":"الاسم بعد the … of."},{"q":"The river is 2 kilometers ___.","options":["long","longly","lengthen","length"],"answer":"long","explanation":"After the number, use the adjective (long, high, wide, deep).","explanation_ar":"الصفة بعد الرقم."},{"q":"The ___ of the lake is 10 meters.","options":["deepen","deep","depth","deeply"],"answer":"depth","explanation":"Use the measurement noun after \"the … of\".","explanation_ar":"الاسم بعد the … of."},{"q":"Weightlifters need a lot of ___.","options":["strong","strongly","strengthen","strength"],"answer":"strength","explanation":"Choose the word-family member that fits (noun, verb, adjective).","explanation_ar":"اختر فرد العائلة المناسب."},{"q":"The workers are going to ___ the narrow street.","options":["wide","width","widen","widely"],"answer":"widen","explanation":"Choose the word-family member that fits (noun, verb, adjective).","explanation_ar":"اختر فرد العائلة المناسب."},{"q":"She ___ the world record in 2024.","options":["did","broke","took","made"],"answer":"broke","explanation":"Record collocations: break/set/hold a record.","explanation_ar":"متلازمات الرقم القياسي."}]},{"id":"GV-L04-U1-LS3-B1","type":"match","instructions":"Guided practice: Match the adjective to the noun.","items":[{"q":"long","options":["height","length","strength","depth","weight","width"],"answer":"length","explanation":"long → length. Use the measurement noun after \"the … of\".","explanation_ar":"الاسم بعد the … of."},{"q":"wide (adjective)","options":["height","length","strength","depth","weight","width"],"answer":"width","explanation":"wide (adjective) → width. Use the measurement noun after \"the … of\".","explanation_ar":"الاسم بعد the … of."},{"q":"deep","options":["height","length","strength","depth","weight","width"],"answer":"depth","explanation":"deep → depth. Use the measurement noun after \"the … of\".","explanation_ar":"الاسم بعد the … of."},{"q":"strong","options":["height","length","strength","depth","weight","width"],"answer":"strength","explanation":"strong → strength. Use the measurement noun after \"the … of\".","explanation_ar":"الاسم بعد the … of."},{"q":"high","options":["height","length","strength","depth","weight","width"],"answer":"height","explanation":"high → height. Use the measurement noun after \"the … of\".","explanation_ar":"الاسم بعد the … of."},{"q":"heavy","options":["height","length","strength","depth","weight","width"],"answer":"weight","explanation":"heavy → weight. Use the measurement noun after \"the … of\".","explanation_ar":"الاسم بعد the … of."}]},{"id":"GV-L04-U1-LS3-C1","type":"open","instructions":"Freer practice: Write measurement facts.","items":[{"q":"My height is about ___.","options":[],"answer":"My height is about 140 centimeters.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses measurement nouns from adjectives (high → height, long → length, strong → strength); record words; units correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"The length of my classroom is about ___.","options":[],"answer":"The length of my classroom is about 8 meters.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses measurement nouns from adjectives (high → height, long → length, strong → strength); record words; units correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"My school bag's weight is about ___.","options":[],"answer":"My school bag's weight is about 4 kilograms.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses measurement nouns from adjectives (high → height, long → length, strong → strength); record words; units correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"The fastest speed of a car on the highway is ___.","options":[],"answer":"The fastest speed on the highway is 120 kilometers per hour.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses measurement nouns from adjectives (high → height, long → length, strong → strength); record words; units correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"A record I want to break is ___.","options":[],"answer":"A record I want to break is the school record for running.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses measurement nouns from adjectives (high → height, long → length, strong → strength); record words; units correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."}]},{"id":"GV-L04-U1-LS3-D1","type":"open","instructions":"Production: Record report.","items":[{"q":"Measure 3 things in the classroom. Write their length, width or height.","options":[],"answer":"The board is 3 meters long. The door is 1 meter wide. The window is 1.5 meters high.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses measurement nouns from adjectives (high → height, long → length, strong → strength); record words; units correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Write 2 sentences with the … of.","options":[],"answer":"The height of the door is 2 meters. The length of the table is 1.5 meters.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses measurement nouns from adjectives (high → height, long → length, strong → strength); record words; units correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Write one sentence about a champion you admire.","options":[],"answer":"Ali is the champion of our school chess club.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses measurement nouns from adjectives (high → height, long → length, strong → strength); record words; units correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."}]}],"game":{"name":"Word Family Tree","mechanic":"drag_and_drop","rules":["Teams take turns drawing a word card.","Place the card on the correct branch of the tree and say a sentence with it.","Correct placement and sentence = 2 points.","The team with the most points when the tree is full wins."],"data":[{"word":"height","category":"noun","family":"high"},{"word":"highly","category":"adverb","family":"high"},{"word":"length","category":"noun","family":"long"},{"word":"lengthen","category":"verb","family":"long"},{"word":"width","category":"noun","family":"wide"},{"word":"widen","category":"verb","family":"wide"},{"word":"depth","category":"noun","family":"deep"},{"word":"deepen","category":"verb","family":"deep"},{"word":"strength","category":"noun","family":"strong"},{"word":"strengthen","category":"verb","family":"strong"}]},"exit_quiz":[{"q":"The ___ of the swimming pool is 50 meters.","options":["lengthen","longly","length","long"],"answer":"length","explanation":"Use the measurement noun after \"the … of\".","explanation_ar":"الاسم بعد the … of."},{"q":"The table is 80 centimeters ___.","options":["wide","widen","width","widely"],"answer":"wide","explanation":"After the number, use the adjective (long, high, wide, deep).","explanation_ar":"الصفة بعد الرقم."},{"q":"The noun from \"deep\" is ___.","options":["deeply","deepness","depth","deepen"],"answer":"depth","explanation":"Choose the word-family member that fits (noun, verb, adjective).","explanation_ar":"اختر فرد العائلة المناسب."},{"q":"A cheetah's top ___ is about 110 km/h.","options":["fast","rapid","speed","quickly"],"answer":"speed","explanation":"Use the measurement noun after \"the … of\".","explanation_ar":"الاسم بعد the … of."},{"q":"We measure weight in ___.","options":["kilograms","degrees","kilometers per hour","meters"],"answer":"kilograms","explanation":"Choose the right unit (meters, kilograms, km/h).","explanation_ar":"اختر وحدة القياس."},{"q":"Exercise can ___ your muscles.","options":["strong","strongly","strength","strengthen"],"answer":"strengthen","explanation":"Choose the word-family member that fits (noun, verb, adjective).","explanation_ar":"اختر فرد العائلة المناسب."},{"q":"","options":["The tower is 828 meters highly.","The tower is 828 meters height.","The tower is 828 meters heighten.","The tower is 828 meters high."],"answer":"The tower is 828 meters high.","explanation":"After the number, use the adjective (long, high, wide, deep).","explanation_ar":"الصفة بعد الرقم."},{"q":"The swimmer ___ a new national record.","options":["did","set","took","made up"],"answer":"set","explanation":"Record collocations: break/set/hold a record.","explanation_ar":"متلازمات الرقم القياسي."},{"q":"The verb from \"long\" is ___.","options":["longly","lengthen","longen","length"],"answer":"lengthen","explanation":"Choose the word-family member that fits (noun, verb, adjective).","explanation_ar":"اختر فرد العائلة المناسب."},{"q":"The person who wins a competition is the ___.","options":["champion","record","height","tower"],"answer":"champion","explanation":"Record collocations: break/set/hold a record.","explanation_ar":"متلازمات الرقم القياسي."}],"images":[{"id":"GV-L04-U1-LS3-IMG01","prompt":"A record board in a science museum showing a measuring tape, a scale, a speedometer and labels for height, length, weight and speed next to giant animals. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Landscape 16:9.","alt":"A record board in a science museum showing a measuring tape, a scale, a speedometer and labels for height, length, weight and speed next to giant animals"},{"id":"GV-L04-U1-LS3-IMG02","prompt":"word-web visual: a central circle with branches to 5 small picture icons of the lesson words; empty labels. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"word-web visual: a central circle with branches to 5 small picture icons of the lesson words"},{"id":"GV-L04-U1-LS3-W01","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows kilogram (a measure of weight; 1,000 grams); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing kilogram: a measure of weight; 1,000 grams"},{"id":"GV-L04-U1-LS3-W02","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows tower (a very tall, narrow building); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing tower: a very tall, narrow building"},{"id":"GV-L04-U1-LS3-W03","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows fountain (a structure that sends water up into the air); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing fountain: a structure that sends water up into the air"},{"id":"GV-L04-U1-LS3-W04","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows giant (very, very big); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing giant: very, very big"},{"id":"GV-L04-U1-LS3-W05","prompt":"Single clear picture that shows amazing (very surprising and wonderful); centred subject, simple light background. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"Picture showing amazing: very surprising and wonderful"},{"id":"GV-L04-U1-LS3-G01","prompt":"Card-back and board design for the classroom game “Word Family Tree”: Zaki the Falcon icon in the centre, Leaf Green border with navy stars. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image. Portrait 2:3.","alt":"Game card design for Word Family Tree"}],"audio":[{"id":"AUD-GV-L04-U1-LS3-W01","script":"kilogram. kilogram. This watermelon weighs five kilograms.","voice":"en-US, warm female or male teacher voice","speed":"0.9"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L04-U1-LS3-W02","script":"tower. tower. The TV tower in Riyadh is very tall.","voice":"en-US, warm female or male teacher voice","speed":"0.9"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L04-U1-LS3-W03","script":"fountain. fountain. The fountain in the park lights up at night.","voice":"en-US, warm female or male teacher voice","speed":"0.9"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L04-U1-LS3-W04","script":"giant. giant. A giant tortoise can live for 150 years.","voice":"en-US, warm female or male teacher voice","speed":"0.9"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L04-U1-LS3-W05","script":"amazing. amazing. The view from the top was amazing.","voice":"en-US, warm female or male teacher voice","speed":"0.9"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L04-U1-LS3-VID","script":"Hi, I’m Zaki! Today’s lesson is “Height, Length, Speed: Measurement Words and Word Families”. Let’s learn measurement nouns from adjectives (high → height, long → length, strong → strength); record words; units together. Meet some new words. kilogram: a measure of weight; 1,000 grams. tower: a very tall, narrow building. fountain: a structure that sends water up into the air. Many measurement nouns come from adjectives: high → height, long → length, wide → width, deep → depth, strong → strength, heavy → weight, fast → speed. Use the noun with the … of: The length of the river is 6,650 kilometers. Use the adjective with be: The river is 6,650 kilometers long. Here are some examples. The height of Jabal Sawda is about 3,000 meters. The road is 20 meters wide. The depth of the pool is two meters. Be careful! Some learners say: “The long of the river is 50 km.” That’s not right. We say: “The length of the river is 50 km.” Use the noun length after the … of. Quick check: What is the noun from \"strong\"? … Think! … *strength*. Great job! Now you can say: I can say \"The height of the tower is 828 meters.\"","voice":"en-US, Zaki the Falcon narrator voice (bright, friendly)","speed":"0.9"}]},{"id":"GV-L04-U1-LS4","title":"\"The Lost Falcon\": Capitalizing Titles","objectives":["Students will be able to capitalize the important words in titles.","Students will be able to keep small words (a, the, of, in, and) lowercase unless they come first or last.","I can write titles like \"The Boy and the Giant Tower\".","I can write the names of famous places correctly."],"objectives_ar":["سيتمكن الطلاب من كتابة الكلمات المهمة في العناوين بحرف كبير.","سيتمكن الطلاب من إبقاء الكلمات الصغيرة بحرف صغير إلا إذا جاءت أولًا أو أخيرًا.","أستطيع أن أكتب عناوين مثل The Boy and the Giant Tower.","أستطيع أن أكتب أسماء الأماكن الشهيرة بشكل صحيح."],"vocabulary":[{"word":"record","pos":"noun","ipa":"/rəˈkɔrd/","definition":"the best result that anyone has ever had","arabic":"رقم قياسي","example":"She broke the school record for running.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"champion","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈtʃæmpiən/","definition":"a person or team that wins a competition","arabic":"بطل","example":"The champion lifted the gold cup.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"height","pos":"noun","ipa":"/haɪt/","definition":"how tall or high something is","arabic":"ارتفاع / طول","example":"The height of the tower is 828 meters.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"length","pos":"noun","ipa":"/lɛŋkθ/","definition":"how long something is","arabic":"طول","example":"The length of the river is 6,650 kilometers.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"weight","pos":"noun","ipa":"/weɪt/","definition":"how heavy something is","arabic":"وزن","example":"The weight of a blue whale is about 150 tons.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"speed","pos":"noun","ipa":"/spid/","definition":"how fast something moves","arabic":"سرعة","example":"A cheetah can reach a speed of 110 kilometers per hour.","image_id":"","audio_id":""}],"explanation":{"text":"In a title, start the first word, the last word and all important words (nouns, verbs, adjectives, pronouns, adverbs) with a capital letter: The Lost Falcon, A Journey to the Stars.\nKeep small words lowercase in the middle: a, an, the, and, but, or, of, in, on, at, to, for, with. Example: The Boy and the Giant Tower.\nNames of famous places and buildings also need capitals: the Burj Khalifa, King Fahd's Fountain, the Red Sea. The word the before a place is usually small.\nCapitalize the first and last word of a title.\nCapitalize important words: nouns, verbs, adjectives, adverbs, pronouns.\nSmall words (a, an, the, and, but, or, of, in, on, to, for) → lowercase in the middle.\nFamous places: the Burj Khalifa, the Red Sea, Masmak Fortress.","examples":["My favorite story is The Fastest Camel in the Desert.","We read a poem called Rain on the Mountain.","Have you seen the film A Trip to the Moon?","The Burj Khalifa is in Dubai.","We visited Masmak Fortress in Riyadh.","The book How to Break a Record is in the library.","The Red Sea has beautiful coral.","Our class play is The King and the Wise Girl."],"common_errors":["✗ the lost falcon → ✓ The Lost Falcon (Capitalize the first word and important words.)","✗ A Trip To The Moon → ✓ A Trip to the Moon (Small words stay lowercase in the middle.)","✗ The Boy and the giant tower → ✓ The Boy and the Giant Tower (Giant and Tower are important words.)","✗ the burj khalifa → ✓ the Burj Khalifa (Names of buildings need capitals.)"],"arabic":"في العناوين نكتب الكلمة الأولى والأخيرة والكلمات المهمة بحرف كبير: The Lost Falcon.\nالكلمات الصغيرة مثل a وthe وand وof وin تبقى صغيرة في وسط العنوان.\nأسماء الأماكن والمباني الشهيرة بحرف كبير: the Burj Khalifa وthe Red Sea."},"video":{"script":[{"time":"00:00–00:20","narration":"Hi, I’m Zaki! Today’s lesson is “\"The Lost Falcon\": Capitalizing Titles”. Let’s learn capital letters in titles of books, stories, films and poems; names of famous places together.","on_screen":"GV-L04-U1-LS4 | \"The Lost Falcon\": Capitalizing Titles","visual":"Zaki the Falcon flies in over the Leaf Green title card and lands next to the lesson title; soft chime."},{"time":"00:20–00:45","narration":"In a title, start the first word, the last word and all important words (nouns, verbs, adjectives, pronouns, adverbs) with a capital letter: The Lost Falcon, A Journey to the Stars.","on_screen":"capital letters in titles of books, stories, films and poems; names of famous places","visual":"Pattern strips slide in from the left; the key words are highlighted in Leaf Green."},{"time":"00:45–01:30","narration":"In a title, start the first word, the last word and all important words (nouns, verbs, adjectives, pronouns, adverbs) with a capital letter: The Lost Falcon, A Journey to the Stars. Keep small words lowercase in the middle: a, an, the, and, but, or, of, in, on, at, to, for, with. Example: The Boy and the Giant Tower.","on_screen":"Capitalize the first and last word of a title. • Capitalize important words: nouns, verbs, adjectives, adverbs, pronouns. • Small words (a, an, the, and, but, or, of, in, on, to, for) → lowercase in the middle.","visual":"Grammar box builds line by line (form → meaning → use); Zaki points to each line."},{"time":"01:30–02:15","narration":"Here are some examples. My favorite story is The Fastest Camel in the Desert. We read a poem called Rain on the Mountain. Have you seen the film A Trip to the Moon?","on_screen":"My favorite story is The Fastest Camel in the Desert. / We read a poem called Rain on the Mountain. / Have you seen the film A Trip to the Moon?","visual":"Each example appears on a card with a small picture; the target part bounces once and turns green."},{"time":"02:15–02:45","narration":"Be careful! Some learners say: “the lost falcon.” That’s not right. We say: “The Lost Falcon.” Capitalize the first word and important words.","on_screen":"✗ the lost falcon   ✓ The Lost Falcon","visual":"A red cross stamps the wrong sentence; it slides away and the correct sentence appears with a green tick."},{"time":"02:45–03:05","narration":"Quick check: Does \"of\" need a capital in the middle of a title? … Think! … No. Great job! Now you can say: I can write titles like \"The Boy and the Giant Tower\".","on_screen":"Quick check ✔  |  I can: I can write titles like \"The Boy and the Giant Tower\".","visual":"Three-second pause with a countdown ring; Zaki gives a wing \"thumbs up\" and confetti in the programme colours."}],"captions_ar":["مرحبًا، أنا زكي! درس اليوم: capital letters in titles of books, stories, films and poems; names of famous places.","استمع وانتبه إلى الكلمات الملوّنة بالأخضر.","في العناوين نكتب الكلمة الأولى والأخيرة والكلمات المهمة بحرف كبير: The Lost Falcon.","لاحظ الأمثلة: الجزء الملوّن هو القاعدة.","انتبه! الخطأ: the lost falcon — الصحيح: The Lost Falcon","سؤال سريع… فكّر ثم أجب. أحسنت! الآن تستطيع: أستطيع أن أكتب عناوين مثل The Boy and the Giant Tower."]},"texts":[{"type":"reading","title":"Our Class Library List (editing passage)","body":"This month we are reading the Giant Tortoise, A Journey To the Ocean, and The Champion Of the Desert Race. We also have a book about the burj Khalifa and one called How to build a Tower.","word_count":37,"audio_id":""}],"activities":[{"id":"GV-L04-U1-LS4-A1","type":"mcq","instructions":"Controlled practice: Choose the correctly written title.","items":[{"q":"","options":["the Secret of the Old Well","The Secret Of The Old Well","The Secret of the Old Well","The secret of the old well"],"answer":"The Secret of the Old Well","explanation":"Small words stay lowercase in the middle.","explanation_ar":"الكلمات الصغيرة بحرف صغير."},{"q":"","options":["A day at the camel race","a Day at the Camel Race","A Day at the Camel Race","A Day At The Camel Race"],"answer":"A Day at the Camel Race","explanation":"Capitalize the first and last words of a title.","explanation_ar":"الكلمة الأولى والأخيرة بحرف كبير."},{"q":"","options":["The Girl Who Loved Stars","The Girl who Loved stars","The girl who loved stars","the Girl Who Loved Stars"],"answer":"The Girl Who Loved Stars","explanation":"Capitalize important words (nouns, verbs, adjectives).","explanation_ar":"الكلمات المهمة بحرف كبير."},{"q":"","options":["Lost In The Desert","Lost in the Desert","Lost in the desert","lost in the desert"],"answer":"Lost in the Desert","explanation":"Small words stay lowercase in the middle.","explanation_ar":"الكلمات الصغيرة بحرف صغير."},{"q":"","options":["We visited the burj khalifa.","We visited the Burj khalifa.","We visited The Burj khalifa.","We visited the Burj Khalifa."],"answer":"We visited the Burj Khalifa.","explanation":"Famous places and buildings need capital letters.","explanation_ar":"الأماكن الشهيرة بحرف كبير."},{"q":"","options":["Running for the gold cup","Running for the Gold Cup","running for the gold cup","Running For The Gold Cup"],"answer":"Running for the Gold Cup","explanation":"Capitalize important words (nouns, verbs, adjectives).","explanation_ar":"الكلمات المهمة بحرف كبير."}]},{"id":"GV-L04-U1-LS4-B1","type":"open","instructions":"Guided practice: Correct the title.","items":[{"q":"My favorite book is the Clever Merchant.","options":[],"answer":"My favorite book is The Clever Merchant.","explanation":"the → The. Capitalize the first and last words of a title.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: the → The. الكلمة الأولى والأخيرة بحرف كبير."},{"q":"The poem is called Night On the Dunes.","options":[],"answer":"The poem is called Night on the Dunes.","explanation":"On → on. Small words stay lowercase in the middle.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: On → on. الكلمات الصغيرة بحرف صغير."},{"q":"We watched The Fastest car in the World.","options":[],"answer":"We watched The Fastest Car in the World.","explanation":"car → Car. Capitalize important words (nouns, verbs, adjectives).","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: car → Car. الكلمات المهمة بحرف كبير."},{"q":"The story Of the Brave Pearl Diver is exciting.","options":[],"answer":"The story of the Brave Pearl Diver is exciting.","explanation":"Of → of. Small words stay lowercase in the middle.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: Of → of. الكلمات الصغيرة بحرف صغير."},{"q":"We swam in the red sea.","options":[],"answer":"We swam in the Red Sea.","explanation":"red sea → Red Sea. Famous places and buildings need capital letters.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: red sea → Red Sea. الأماكن الشهيرة بحرف كبير."},{"q":"Read the chapter \"Climbing the Highest mountain.\"","options":[],"answer":"Read the chapter \"Climbing the Highest Mountain.\"","explanation":"mountain → Mountain. Capitalize important words (nouns, verbs, adjectives).","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: mountain → Mountain. الكلمات المهمة بحرف كبير."}]},{"id":"GV-L04-U1-LS4-C1","type":"open","instructions":"Freer practice: Edit the library list.","items":[{"q":"This month we are reading the Giant Tortoise, A Journey to the Ocean, and The Champion of the Desert Race.","options":[],"answer":"This month we are reading The Giant Tortoise, A Journey to the Ocean, and The Champion of the Desert Race.","explanation":"the → The. Capitalize the first and last words of a title.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: the → The. الكلمة الأولى والأخيرة بحرف كبير."},{"q":"This month we are reading The Giant Tortoise, A Journey To the Ocean, and The Champion of the Desert Race.","options":[],"answer":"This month we are reading The Giant Tortoise, A Journey to the Ocean, and The Champion of the Desert Race.","explanation":"To → to. Capitalize the first and last words of a title.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: To → to. الكلمة الأولى والأخيرة بحرف كبير."},{"q":"This month we are reading The Giant Tortoise, A Journey to the Ocean, and The Champion Of the Desert Race.","options":[],"answer":"This month we are reading The Giant Tortoise, A Journey to the Ocean, and The Champion of the Desert Race.","explanation":"Of → of. Capitalize the first and last words of a title.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: Of → of. الكلمة الأولى والأخيرة بحرف كبير."},{"q":"We also have a book about the burj Khalifa and one called How to Build a Tower.","options":[],"answer":"We also have a book about the Burj Khalifa and one called How to Build a Tower.","explanation":"burj → Burj. Capitalize the first and last words of a title.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: burj → Burj. الكلمة الأولى والأخيرة بحرف كبير."},{"q":"We also have a book about the Burj Khalifa and one called How to build a Tower.","options":[],"answer":"We also have a book about the Burj Khalifa and one called How to Build a Tower.","explanation":"build → Build. Capitalize the first and last words of a title.","explanation_ar":"التصحيح: build → Build. الكلمة الأولى والأخيرة بحرف كبير."}]},{"id":"GV-L04-U1-LS4-D1","type":"open","instructions":"Production: Write titles.","items":[{"q":"Write a title for a story about a record-breaking camel.","options":[],"answer":"The Fastest Camel in Arabia","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses capital letters in titles of books, stories, films and poems; names of famous places correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Write a title for a poem about the sea.","options":[],"answer":"Waves on the Red Sea","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses capital letters in titles of books, stories, films and poems; names of famous places correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Write the title of a book you like (or invent one) with \"of\" or \"and\" in it.","options":[],"answer":"The Lion and the Little Mouse","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses capital letters in titles of books, stories, films and poems; names of famous places correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."}]}],"game":{"name":"Spelling Relay","mechanic":"word_builder","rules":["Teams line up facing the board.","The teacher says a word; the first student runs to the board and writes the first letter.","The next student adds the next letter, and so on.","The first team with the correct spelling wins the point."],"data":[{"word":"record","clue":"the best result that anyone has ever had"},{"word":"champion","clue":"a person or team that wins a competition"},{"word":"height","clue":"how tall or high something is"},{"word":"length","clue":"how long something is"},{"word":"kilometer","clue":"a measure of distance; 1,000 meters"},{"word":"amazing","clue":"very surprising and wonderful"},{"word":"weight","clue":"how heavy something is"},{"word":"speed","clue":"how fast something moves"},{"word":"meter","clue":"a measure of length; 100 centimeters"},{"word":"kilogram","clue":"a measure of weight; 1,000 grams"},{"word":"tower","clue":"a very tall, narrow building"}]},"exit_quiz":[{"q":"","options":["The Boy and the Falcon","The Boy And The Falcon","the boy and the falcon","The boy and the Falcon"],"answer":"The Boy and the Falcon","explanation":"Small words stay lowercase in the middle.","explanation_ar":"الكلمات الصغيرة بحرف صغير."},{"q":"","options":["Under The Desert Stars","Under the Desert Stars","under the desert stars","Under the desert stars"],"answer":"Under the Desert Stars","explanation":"Capitalize important words (nouns, verbs, adjectives).","explanation_ar":"الكلمات المهمة بحرف كبير."},{"q":"Which word stays lowercase in a title?","options":["Desert","of","Stars","Running"],"answer":"of","explanation":"Small words stay lowercase in the middle.","explanation_ar":"الكلمات الصغيرة بحرف صغير."},{"q":"","options":["A tower in the clouds","a Tower in the Clouds","A Tower in the Clouds","A Tower In The Clouds"],"answer":"A Tower in the Clouds","explanation":"Capitalize the first and last words of a title.","explanation_ar":"الكلمة الأولى والأخيرة بحرف كبير."},{"q":"","options":["We went to King Fahd's fountain.","We went to king fahd's fountain.","We went to king Fahd's Fountain.","We went to King Fahd's Fountain."],"answer":"We went to King Fahd's Fountain.","explanation":"Famous places and buildings need capital letters.","explanation_ar":"الأماكن الشهيرة بحرف كبير."},{"q":"How many words need a capital? \"the girl who climbed the mountain\"","options":["5","3","4","6"],"answer":"5","explanation":"Capitalize important words (nouns, verbs, adjectives).","explanation_ar":"الكلمات المهمة بحرف كبير."},{"q":"","options":["how the Camel Got Its Hump","How the Camel Got Its Hump","How the camel got its hump","How The Camel Got Its Hump"],"answer":"How the Camel Got Its Hump","explanation":"Capitalize important words (nouns, verbs, adjectives).","explanation_ar":"الكلمات المهمة بحرف كبير."},{"q":"","options":["Masmak Fortress is in riyadh.","masmak Fortress is in Riyadh.","Masmak Fortress is in Riyadh.","Masmak fortress is in Riyadh."],"answer":"Masmak Fortress is in Riyadh.","explanation":"Famous places and buildings need capital letters.","explanation_ar":"الأماكن الشهيرة بحرف كبير."},{"q":"In a title, which word needs a capital in the middle?","options":["Tower","the","of","and"],"answer":"Tower","explanation":"Capitalize important words (nouns, verbs, adjectives).","explanation_ar":"الكلمات المهمة بحرف كبير."},{"q":"","options":["Champions of the world","Champions Of The World","champions of the world","Champions of the World"],"answer":"Champions of the World","explanation":"Small words stay lowercase in the middle.","explanation_ar":"الكلمات الصغيرة بحرف صغير."}],"images":[{"id":"GV-L04-U1-LS4-IMG01","prompt":"Two or three of the programme characters in a scene about “Record Breakers” that shows capital letters in titles of books, stories, films and poems; names of famous places in action. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Landscape 16:9.","alt":"Two or three of the programme characters in a scene about “Record Breakers” that shows capital letters in titles of books, stories, films and poems; names of famous places in action"},{"id":"GV-L04-U1-LS4-IMG02","prompt":"friendly editing-desk scene: a magnifying glass over a page with highlighted punctuation marks, Zaki holding a green pen. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"friendly editing-desk scene: a magnifying glass over a page with highlighted punctuation marks, Zaki holding a green pen"},{"id":"GV-L04-U1-LS4-G01","prompt":"Card-back and board design for the classroom game “Spelling Relay”: Zaki the Falcon icon in the centre, Leaf Green border with navy stars. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image. Portrait 2:3.","alt":"Game card design for Spelling Relay"}],"audio":[{"id":"AUD-GV-L04-U1-LS4-VID","script":"Hi, I’m Zaki! Today’s lesson is “\"The Lost Falcon\": Capitalizing Titles”. Let’s learn capital letters in titles of books, stories, films and poems; names of famous places together. In a title, start the first word, the last word and all important words (nouns, verbs, adjectives, pronouns, adverbs) with a capital letter: The Lost Falcon, A Journey to the Stars. In a title, start the first word, the last word and all important words (nouns, verbs, adjectives, pronouns, adverbs) with a capital letter: The Lost Falcon, A Journey to the Stars. Keep small words lowercase in the middle: a, an, the, and, but, or, of, in, on, at, to, for, with. Example: The Boy and the Giant Tower. Here are some examples. My favorite story is The Fastest Camel in the Desert. We read a poem called Rain on the Mountain. Have you seen the film A Trip to the Moon? Be careful! Some learners say: “the lost falcon.” That’s not right. We say: “The Lost Falcon.” Capitalize the first word and important words. Quick check: Does \"of\" need a capital in the middle of a title? … Think! … No. Great job! Now you can say: I can write titles like \"The Boy and the Giant Tower\".","voice":"en-US, Zaki the Falcon narrator voice (bright, friendly)","speed":"0.9"}]},{"id":"GV-L04-U1-LS5","title":"Our Book of Records: Language in Use","objectives":["Students will be able to present class and world records.","Students will be able to write a record fact sheet with superlatives, measurements and a correctly capitalized title.","I can present amazing records.","I can write a fact sheet for our Book of Records."],"objectives_ar":["سيتمكن الطلاب من عرض أرقام قياسية للصف والعالم.","سيتمكن الطلاب من كتابة صحيفة حقائق عن الأرقام القياسية مع صيغ التفضيل والقياسات وعنوان صحيح.","أستطيع أن أعرض أرقامًا قياسية مدهشة.","أستطيع أن أكتب صحيفة حقائق لكتاب الأرقام القياسية."],"vocabulary":[{"word":"record","pos":"noun","ipa":"/rəˈkɔrd/","definition":"the best result that anyone has ever had","arabic":"رقم قياسي","example":"She broke the school record for running.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"champion","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈtʃæmpiən/","definition":"a person or team that wins a competition","arabic":"بطل","example":"The champion lifted the gold cup.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"height","pos":"noun","ipa":"/haɪt/","definition":"how tall or high something is","arabic":"ارتفاع / طول","example":"The height of the tower is 828 meters.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"length","pos":"noun","ipa":"/lɛŋkθ/","definition":"how long something is","arabic":"طول","example":"The length of the river is 6,650 kilometers.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"weight","pos":"noun","ipa":"/weɪt/","definition":"how heavy something is","arabic":"وزن","example":"The weight of a blue whale is about 150 tons.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"speed","pos":"noun","ipa":"/spid/","definition":"how fast something moves","arabic":"سرعة","example":"A cheetah can reach a speed of 110 kilometers per hour.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"meter","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈmitɚ/","definition":"a measure of length; 100 centimeters","arabic":"متر","example":"The pool is 50 meters long.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"kilometer","pos":"noun","ipa":"/kəˈlɑmətɚ/","definition":"a measure of distance; 1,000 meters","arabic":"كيلومتر","example":"My school is two kilometers from home.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"kilogram","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈkɪləˌɡræm/","definition":"a measure of weight; 1,000 grams","arabic":"كيلوغرام","example":"This watermelon weighs five kilograms.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"tower","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈtaʊɚ/","definition":"a very tall, narrow building","arabic":"برج","example":"The TV tower in Riyadh is very tall.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"fountain","pos":"noun","ipa":"/ˈfaʊntən/","definition":"a structure that sends water up into the air","arabic":"نافورة","example":"The fountain in the park lights up at night.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"giant","pos":"adjective","ipa":"/ˈdʒaɪənt/","definition":"very, very big","arabic":"عملاق","example":"A giant tortoise can live for 150 years.","image_id":"","audio_id":""},{"word":"amazing","pos":"adjective","ipa":"/əˈmeɪzɪŋ/","definition":"very surprising and wonderful","arabic":"مذهل","example":"The view from the top was amazing.","image_id":"","audio_id":""}],"explanation":{"text":"Today you use all of Unit 1: superlatives, comparatives, the least, one of the…, measurement words and capitals in titles.\nA fact sheet has a title, true facts with numbers, and one opinion at the end.\n✔ the + -est / the most / the best, the worst\n✔ comparative + than for two things\n✔ height, length, weight, speed + units\n✔ capitals in the title","examples":["The camel is the largest animal in the desert.","A camel is stronger than a donkey.","Its weight can be 600 kilograms.","It is one of the most useful animals in the world.","Camels can live for the longest time without water.","The height of a camel is about two meters.","This is the least known camel fact.","My fact sheet is called The Ship of the Desert."],"common_errors":["✗ The camel is the most strong animal. → ✓ The camel is the strongest animal. (Short adjective → -est.)","✗ It's one of the most useful animal. → ✓ It's one of the most useful animals. (Plural after one of the.)","✗ the ship of the desert → ✓ The Ship of the Desert (Capitals in the title.)"],"arabic":"نراجع صيغ التفضيل والمقارنة وone of the وكلمات القياس والحروف الكبيرة في العناوين.\nصحيفة الحقائق لها عنوان وحقائق صحيحة بالأرقام ورأي واحد في النهاية.\nتذكّر: the قبل صيغة التفضيل، والجمع بعد one of the."},"video":{"script":[{"time":"00:00–00:20","narration":"Hi, I’m Zaki! Today’s lesson is “Our Book of Records: Language in Use”. Let’s learn superlatives vs comparatives, one of the, measurement words and capitalizing titles (unit review) together.","on_screen":"GV-L04-U1-LS5 | Our Book of Records: Language in Use","visual":"Zaki the Falcon flies in over the Leaf Green title card and lands next to the lesson title; soft chime."},{"time":"00:20–00:45","narration":"Let’s use everything from this unit. Your task: Record quiz show: teams write 5 quiz questions with superlatives (\"What is the longest river in the world?\"). Other teams answer with full sentences. Score a bonus point for using a measurement word.","on_screen":"Language in use","visual":"Split screen: two cast members talking, with speech bubbles appearing."},{"time":"00:45–01:30","narration":"Today you use all of Unit 1: superlatives, comparatives, the least, one of the…, measurement words and capitals in titles. A fact sheet has a title, true facts with numbers, and one opinion at the end.","on_screen":"✔ the + -est / the most / the best, the worst • ✔ comparative + than for two things • ✔ height, length, weight, speed + units","visual":"Grammar box builds line by line (form → meaning → use); Zaki points to each line."},{"time":"01:30–02:15","narration":"Here are some examples. The camel is the largest animal in the desert. A camel is stronger than a donkey. Its weight can be 600 kilograms.","on_screen":"The camel is the largest animal in the desert. / A camel is stronger than a donkey. / Its weight can be 600 kilograms.","visual":"Each example appears on a card with a small picture; the target part bounces once and turns green."},{"time":"02:15–02:45","narration":"Be careful! Some learners say: “The camel is the most strong animal.” That’s not right. We say: “The camel is the strongest animal.” Short adjective → -est.","on_screen":"✗ The camel is the most strong animal.   ✓ The camel is the strongest animal.","visual":"A red cross stamps the wrong sentence; it slides away and the correct sentence appears with a green tick."},{"time":"02:45–03:05","narration":"Quick check: what is wrong with “It's one of the most useful animal.”? … Think! … It should be “It's one of the most useful animals.”. Great job! Now you can say: I can present amazing records.","on_screen":"Quick check ✔  |  I can: I can present amazing records.","visual":"Three-second pause with a countdown ring; Zaki gives a wing \"thumbs up\" and confetti in the programme colours."}],"captions_ar":["مرحبًا، أنا زكي! درس اليوم: superlatives vs comparatives, one of the, measurement words and capitalizing titles (unit review).","استمع وانتبه إلى الكلمات الملوّنة بالأخضر.","نراجع صيغ التفضيل والمقارنة وone of the وكلمات القياس والحروف الكبيرة في العناوين.","لاحظ الأمثلة: الجزء الملوّن هو القاعدة.","انتبه! الخطأ: The camel is the most strong animal. — الصحيح: The camel is the strongest animal.","سؤال سريع… فكّر ثم أجب. أحسنت! الآن تستطيع: أستطيع أن أعرض أرقامًا قياسية مدهشة."]},"texts":[{"type":"model","title":"The Amazing Arabian Camel – Noura","body":"The camel is one of the most important animals in Arabia.\nIt is the largest animal in the Saudi desert. Its height can be over two meters, and its weight can be 600 kilograms.\nA camel can walk farther than a horse in the hot sand.\nIt can drink about 100 liters of water in ten minutes – that's one of the fastest drinking records in the animal world!\nFor me, the camel is the most amazing animal of all.","word_count":80,"audio_id":"AUD-GV-L04-U1-LS5-T1"}],"activities":[{"id":"GV-L04-U1-LS5-A1","type":"true_false","instructions":"Controlled practice: Read Noura's fact sheet. True or False?","items":[{"q":"The camel is the largest animal in the Saudi desert.","options":["True","False"],"answer":"True","explanation":"Check the text “The Amazing Arabian Camel – Noura”.","explanation_ar":"ارجع إلى النص وابحث عن الجملة التي تعطي الإجابة."},{"q":"A camel's weight can be 6,000 kilograms.","options":["True","False"],"answer":"False","explanation":"Check the text “The Amazing Arabian Camel – Noura”.","explanation_ar":"ارجع إلى النص وابحث عن الجملة التي تعطي الإجابة."},{"q":"A camel can walk farther than a horse in the hot sand.","options":["True","False"],"answer":"True","explanation":"Check the text “The Amazing Arabian Camel – Noura”.","explanation_ar":"ارجع إلى النص وابحث عن الجملة التي تعطي الإجابة."},{"q":"A camel can drink about 100 liters of water in ten minutes.","options":["True","False"],"answer":"True","explanation":"Check the text “The Amazing Arabian Camel – Noura”.","explanation_ar":"ارجع إلى النص وابحث عن الجملة التي تعطي الإجابة."},{"q":"Noura thinks the camel is the least amazing animal.","options":["True","False"],"answer":"False","explanation":"Check the text “The Amazing Arabian Camel – Noura”.","explanation_ar":"ارجع إلى النص وابحث عن الجملة التي تعطي الإجابة."},{"q":"The height of a camel can be over two meters.","options":["True","False"],"answer":"True","explanation":"Check the text “The Amazing Arabian Camel – Noura”.","explanation_ar":"ارجع إلى النص وابحث عن الجملة التي تعطي الإجابة."}]},{"id":"GV-L04-U1-LS5-B1","type":"mcq","instructions":"Guided practice: Choose the correct answer.","items":[{"q":"The camel is ___ animal in the Saudi desert.","options":["larger","largest than","the most large","the largest"],"answer":"the largest","explanation":"Superlative: the -est / the most.","explanation_ar":"صيغة التفضيل."},{"q":"A camel can walk ___ than a horse in the sand.","options":["the farthest","farthest","farther","more far"],"answer":"farther","explanation":"Comparative for two things + than.","explanation_ar":"المقارنة."},{"q":"The camel is one of the most important ___ in Arabia.","options":["animals","animal","animal's","the animal"],"answer":"animals","explanation":"one of the + superlative + plural.","explanation_ar":"one of the + جمع."},{"q":"Its ___ can be 600 kilograms.","options":["height","weight","heavily","heavy"],"answer":"weight","explanation":"Measurement noun or unit.","explanation_ar":"كلمة القياس."},{"q":"","options":["the ship of the desert","The Ship Of The Desert","The Ship of the Desert","The ship of the desert"],"answer":"The Ship of the Desert","explanation":"Capitals in titles.","explanation_ar":"العناوين."},{"q":"The ___ of a camel is about two meters.","options":["height","high","highly","heighten"],"answer":"height","explanation":"Measurement noun or unit.","explanation_ar":"كلمة القياس."}]},{"id":"GV-L04-U1-LS5-C1","type":"open","instructions":"Freer practice: Record quiz show. Write your team's questions and the answers.","items":[{"q":"Question with \"the longest\":","options":[],"answer":"What is the longest river in Saudi Arabia? – Saudi Arabia has no permanent rivers!","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses superlatives vs comparatives, one of the, measurement words and capitalizing titles (unit review) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Question with \"the highest\":","options":[],"answer":"What is the highest mountain in the world? – Mount Everest.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses superlatives vs comparatives, one of the, measurement words and capitalizing titles (unit review) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Question with \"the most\":","options":[],"answer":"What is the most popular sport in Saudi Arabia? – Football.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses superlatives vs comparatives, one of the, measurement words and capitalizing titles (unit review) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Question with \"the fastest\":","options":[],"answer":"What is the fastest bird? – The peregrine falcon.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses superlatives vs comparatives, one of the, measurement words and capitalizing titles (unit review) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Question with a measurement word:","options":[],"answer":"What is the height of the Burj Khalifa? – 828 meters.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses superlatives vs comparatives, one of the, measurement words and capitalizing titles (unit review) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."}]},{"id":"GV-L04-U1-LS5-D1","type":"open","instructions":"Production: Write your record fact sheet.","items":[{"q":"Plan: choose a topic (an animal, a building, a place) and 5 facts with numbers.","options":[],"answer":"Topic: Kingdom Centre – height 302 m, 99 floors, one of the tallest in Riyadh, sky bridge","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses superlatives vs comparatives, one of the, measurement words and capitalizing titles (unit review) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Write 6–7 sentences with a capitalized title.","options":[],"answer":"The Tower with the Sky Bridge. Kingdom Centre is one of the most famous towers in Riyadh. Its height is 302 meters. It is taller than many buildings in the city. The sky bridge is the most exciting part. It has the best view of Riyadh.","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses superlatives vs comparatives, one of the, measurement words and capitalizing titles (unit review) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."},{"q":"Check: the + superlative? plural after one of the? capitals in the title? Fix one mistake.","options":[],"answer":"I changed \"one of the tallest tower\" to \"one of the tallest towers\".","explanation":"Answers will vary. Accept any answer that uses superlatives vs comparatives, one of the, measurement words and capitalizing titles (unit review) correctly and makes sense.","explanation_ar":"تختلف الإجابات. تُقبل أي إجابة صحيحة لغويًا تستخدم قاعدة الدرس ومعناها واضح."}]}],"game":{"name":"Board Race Review","mechanic":"timed_quiz","rules":["One student from each team stands at the board.","The teacher says a cue word and a task (meaning, spelling or sentence with superlatives vs comparatives, one of the, measurement words and capitalizing titles (unit review)).","The first correct answer wins a point; rotate players every round.","Play 10 rounds."],"data":[{"cue":"record","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"champion","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"height","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"length","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"weight","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"speed","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"meter","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"kilometer","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"kilogram","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"tower","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"fountain","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"giant","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]},{"cue":"amazing","tasks":["meaning","spelling","sentence"]}]},"exit_quiz":[{"q":"Mount Everest is ___ mountain on Earth.","options":["the highest","higher","highest than","the most high"],"answer":"the highest","explanation":"Superlative: the -est / the most.","explanation_ar":"صيغة التفضيل."},{"q":"A bus is ___ than a car.","options":["longest","longer","the longer","the longest"],"answer":"longer","explanation":"Comparative for two things + than.","explanation_ar":"المقارنة."},{"q":"","options":["Makkah is the one of oldest cities in the world.","Makkah is one of the oldest cities in the world.","Makkah is one of oldest cities in the world.","Makkah is one of the oldest city in the world."],"answer":"Makkah is one of the oldest cities in the world.","explanation":"one of the + superlative + plural.","explanation_ar":"one of the + جمع."},{"q":"The ___ of the road is 30 meters.","options":["widely","widen","wide","width"],"answer":"width","explanation":"Measurement noun or unit.","explanation_ar":"كلمة القياس."},{"q":"","options":["The Fastest Runner In The School","The fastest runner in the school","The Fastest Runner in the School","the Fastest Runner in the School"],"answer":"The Fastest Runner in the School","explanation":"Capitals in titles.","explanation_ar":"العناوين."},{"q":"Of the three bags, the green one is ___.","options":["heaviest than","heavier","the heaviest","the most heavy"],"answer":"the heaviest","explanation":"Superlative: the -est / the most.","explanation_ar":"صيغة التفضيل."},{"q":"This is ___ crowded beach. It's very quiet.","options":["the least","the most","less","lesser"],"answer":"the least","explanation":"Superlative: the -est / the most.","explanation_ar":"صيغة التفضيل."},{"q":"We measure distance in ___.","options":["degrees","kilometers","kilograms","liters"],"answer":"kilometers","explanation":"Measurement noun or unit.","explanation_ar":"كلمة القياس."},{"q":"","options":["It was the worse sandstorm of the year.","It was the baddest sandstorm of the year.","It was worst sandstorm of the year.","It was the worst sandstorm of the year."],"answer":"It was the worst sandstorm of the year.","explanation":"Superlative: the -est / the most.","explanation_ar":"صيغة التفضيل."},{"q":"Pick the best sentence for a fact sheet:","options":["The peregrine falcon is faster bird in the world.","The peregrine falcon is fastest bird of the world.","The peregrine falcon is the most fast bird in the world.","The peregrine falcon is the fastest bird in the world."],"answer":"The peregrine falcon is the fastest bird in the world.","explanation":"Superlative: the -est / the most.","explanation_ar":"صيغة التفضيل."}],"images":[{"id":"GV-L04-U1-LS5-IMG01","prompt":"Lina and Noura making a big \"Book of Records\" scrapbook with photos of tall towers, fast animals and their classmates' records. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Landscape 16:9.","alt":"Lina and Noura making a big \"Book of Records\" scrapbook with photos of tall towers, fast animals and their classmates' records"},{"id":"GV-L04-U1-LS5-IMG02","prompt":"two programme characters doing the speaking task about “Record Breakers”, speech bubbles left empty. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image; characters drawn as children aged 8–12, big friendly eyes, playful composition. Square 1:1.","alt":"two programme characters doing the speaking task about “Record Breakers”, speech bubbles left empty"},{"id":"GV-L04-U1-LS5-G01","prompt":"Card-back and board design for the classroom game “Board Race Review”: Zaki the Falcon icon in the centre, Leaf Green border with navy stars. Clean flat vector illustration, soft rounded outlines (2 px navy #2E3176), gentle flat shading, programme palette: navy #2E3176, coral #E06377, sun gold #F0B232, sky blue #2A90C5, leaf green #3FA66B accent; white or very light background; modest, culturally appropriate clothing for Saudi schools; boys and girls shown in separate groups in school scenes; no text, letters or logos inside the image. Portrait 2:3.","alt":"Game card design for Board Race Review"}],"audio":[{"id":"AUD-GV-L04-U1-LS5-T1","script":"The camel is one of the most important animals in Arabia. It is the largest animal in the Saudi desert. Its height can be over two meters, and its weight can be 600 kilograms. A camel can walk farther than a horse in the hot sand. It can drink about 100 liters of water in ten minutes – that's one of the fastest drinking records in the animal world! For me, the camel is the most amazing animal of all.","voice":"en-US, warm female or male teacher voice","speed":"0.9"},{"id":"AUD-GV-L04-U1-LS5-VID","script":"Hi, I’m Zaki! Today’s lesson is “Our Book of Records: Language in Use”. Let’s learn superlatives vs comparatives, one of the, measurement words and capitalizing titles (unit review) together. Let’s use everything from this unit. Your task: Record quiz show: teams write 5 quiz questions with superlatives (\"What is the longest river in the world?\"). Other teams answer with full sentences. Score a bonus point for using a measurement word. Today you use all of Unit 1: superlatives, comparatives, the least, one of the…, measurement words and capitals in titles. A fact sheet has a title, true facts with numbers, and one opinion at the end. Here are some examples. The camel is the largest animal in the desert. A camel is stronger than a donkey. Its weight can be 600 kilograms. Be careful! Some learners say: “The camel is the most strong animal.” That’s not right. We say: “The camel is the strongest animal.” Short adjective → -est. Quick check: what is wrong with “It's one of the most useful animal.”? … Think! … It should be “It's one of the most useful animals.”. Great job! Now you can say: I can present amazing records.","voice":"en-US, Zaki the Falcon narrator voice (bright, friendly)","speed":"0.9"}]}],"unit_test":[{"q":"The giraffe is ___ animal in the world.","options":["the tallest","taller","the most tall","tallest"],"answer":"the tallest","explanation":"Short adjective → the + -est.","explanation_ar":"الصفة القصيرة ← the + est."},{"q":"This is ___ painting in the museum.","options":["the famousest","more famous","the most famous","most famous than"],"answer":"the most famous","explanation":"Long adjective → the most + adjective.","explanation_ar":"الصفة الطويلة ← the most."},{"q":"My grandma makes ___ coffee in the family.","options":["best of","the goodest","the better","the best"],"answer":"the best","explanation":"good → the best; bad → the worst.","explanation_ar":"صيغ شاذة."},{"q":"","options":["Antarctica is the most windy place on Earth.","Antarctica is the windier place on Earth.","Antarctica is windiest place on Earth.","Antarctica is the windiest place on Earth."],"answer":"Antarctica is the windiest place on Earth.","explanation":"Always use the before a superlative.","explanation_ar":"لا بد من the."},{"q":"Who is the youngest student ___ your school?","options":["in","of","on","at"],"answer":"in","explanation":"in + place or group (in the world, in my class).","explanation_ar":"in مع المكان أو المجموعة."},{"q":"My cousin is ___ than me.","options":["the strongest","strongest","the stronger","stronger"],"answer":"stronger","explanation":"Two things → comparative + than.","explanation_ar":"شيئان ← المقارنة + than."},{"q":"Of the five films, this one was ___.","options":["more boring","boringest","the more boring","the most boring"],"answer":"the most boring","explanation":"Three or more → the + superlative.","explanation_ar":"ثلاثة أو أكثر ← صيغة التفضيل."},{"q":"","options":["It's one of most beautiful mosques in Madinah.","It's one of the most beautiful mosques in Madinah.","It's one the most beautiful mosques in Madinah.","It's one of the most beautiful mosque in Madinah."],"answer":"It's one of the most beautiful mosques in Madinah.","explanation":"one of the + superlative + plural noun.","explanation_ar":"one of the + جمع."},{"q":"This is ___ difficult puzzle. It's very easy.","options":["the least","less","lesser","the most"],"answer":"the least","explanation":"the least = the smallest amount (opposite of the most).","explanation_ar":"the least عكس the most."},{"q":"","options":["The red bike is the fastest than the blue bike.","The red bike is more fast than the blue bike.","The red bike is faster than the blue bike.","The red bike is fastest than the blue bike."],"answer":"The red bike is faster than the blue bike.","explanation":"Two things → comparative + than.","explanation_ar":"شيئان ← المقارنة + than."},{"q":"The ___ of the pool is three meters. Don't jump in!","options":["deep","depth","deepen","deeply"],"answer":"depth","explanation":"Use the measurement noun after \"the … of\".","explanation_ar":"الاسم بعد the … of."},{"q":"The bridge is 500 meters ___.","options":["lengthen","longly","length","long"],"answer":"long","explanation":"After the number, use the adjective (long, high, wide, deep).","explanation_ar":"الصفة بعد الرقم."},{"q":"The noun from \"strong\" is ___.","options":["strength","strongness","strengthen","strongly"],"answer":"strength","explanation":"Choose the word-family member that fits (noun, verb, adjective).","explanation_ar":"اختر فرد العائلة المناسب."},{"q":"We measure speed in ___.","options":["kilograms","meters only","kilometers per hour","liters"],"answer":"kilometers per hour","explanation":"Choose the right unit (meters, kilograms, km/h).","explanation_ar":"اختر وحدة القياس."},{"q":"The runner ___ the world record.","options":["took","broke","made","did"],"answer":"broke","explanation":"Record collocations: break/set/hold a record.","explanation_ar":"متلازمات الرقم القياسي."},{"q":"The verb from \"wide\" is ___.","options":["wideness","widen","width","widely"],"answer":"widen","explanation":"Choose the word-family member that fits (noun, verb, adjective).","explanation_ar":"اختر فرد العائلة المناسب."},{"q":"","options":["The Mystery Of The Missing Map","The mystery of the missing map","The Mystery of the Missing Map","the mystery of the missing map"],"answer":"The Mystery of the Missing Map","explanation":"Small words stay lowercase in the middle.","explanation_ar":"الكلمات الصغيرة بحرف صغير."},{"q":"","options":["A boy who never gave up","A Boy Who Never Gave Up","a Boy Who Never Gave Up","A Boy who never Gave up"],"answer":"A Boy Who Never Gave Up","explanation":"Capitalize important words (nouns, verbs, adjectives).","explanation_ar":"الكلمات المهمة بحرف كبير."},{"q":"Which word stays small in the middle of a title?","options":["Brave","and","Falcon","Ran"],"answer":"and","explanation":"Small words stay lowercase in the middle.","explanation_ar":"الكلمات الصغيرة بحرف صغير."},{"q":"","options":["We saw the Burj Khalifa at night.","We saw the burj khalifa at night.","We saw the Burj khalifa at night.","We saw The burj Khalifa at night."],"answer":"We saw the Burj Khalifa at night.","explanation":"Famous places and buildings need capital letters.","explanation_ar":"الأماكن الشهيرة بحرف كبير."},{"q":"How many words need capitals? \"the cat in the old house\"","options":["6","5","3","4"],"answer":"4","explanation":"Capitalize important words (nouns, verbs, adjectives).","explanation_ar":"الكلمات المهمة بحرف كبير."},{"q":"Pick the best title for a class record book:","options":["The Biggest And Best Records Of Class 4A","the Biggest and Best Records of Class 4A","The Biggest and Best Records of Class 4A","The biggest and best records of class 4a"],"answer":"The Biggest and Best Records of Class 4A","explanation":"Small words stay lowercase in the middle.","explanation_ar":"الكلمات الصغيرة بحرف صغير."},{"q":"How can we fix it? \"riyadh is the most big city in saudi arabia.\"","options":["Riyadh is biggest city in Saudi Arabia.","Riyadh is the most big city in Saudi Arabia.","Riyadh is the biggest city in Saudi Arabia.","riyadh is the biggest city in saudi arabia."],"answer":"Riyadh is the biggest city in Saudi Arabia.","explanation":"Short adjective → the + -est.","explanation_ar":"الصفة القصيرة ← the + est."},{"q":"What is the deepest lake in the world? – ___","options":["Lake Baikal is the deepest lake in the world.","Lake Baikal is the deeper lake in the world.","Lake Baikal is deepest lake in the world.","Lake Baikal is the most deep lake in the world."],"answer":"Lake Baikal is the deepest lake in the world.","explanation":"Short adjective → the + -est.","explanation_ar":"الصفة القصيرة ← the + est."}],"theme_ar":"محطمو الأرقام القياسية","essential_question_ar":"ما الذي يجعل شيئًا الأكبر أو الأسرع أو الأفضل؟","can_do":"I can describe world records and compare three or more things with superlative adjectives.","can_do_ar":"أستطيع أن أصف الأرقام القياسية وأقارن بين ثلاثة أشياء أو أكثر باستخدام صيغ التفضيل."});
